  "body": "While there is already a ```@rel=\"license\"``` option, I think it would be good to have a ```@rel=\"tos\"``` or ```@rel=\"terms\"``` to help locate the terms of service page for any website. And a ```@rel=\"privacy\"``` for privacy policy.\r\n\r\nThe key difference here is that ```@rel=\"license\"``` is about copyright of the document (see [4.6.6.9 Link type \"license\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#link-type-license)) and ```@rel=\"tos\"``` would be about the rules for usage of a web site/service/application (things like warranty, jurisdiction, etc).\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n```html\r\n<link rel=\"tos\" href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/github/site-policy/github-terms-of-service\">\r\n<link rel=\"privacy\" href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/github/site-policy/github-privacy-statement\">\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
